#X obj 2900 2200 text define -k \$0-pad;
#A set 1 48 \; 2 49 \; 3 50 \; 4 51 \; 5 44 \; 6 45 \; 7 46 \; 8 47 \; 9 40 \; 10 41 \; 11 42 \; 12 43 \; 13 36 \; 14 37 \; 15 38 \; 16 39 \;;
#X text 20 20 m_404 -- the Roland SP-404MKII \, and the only file allowed to talk to it. THE FIRST BIDIRECTIONAL DEVICE LAYER: every m_ file before it either only listened (nano \, Launchpad \, Organelle) or only spoke (Volca). This one does both \, over the same sixteen notes on ten channels., f 84;
#X text 20 130 creation arg 1: the Pd channel that the 404's OWN channel 1 -- bank A -- lands on. 33 on the Organelle \, input/output slot 3. REQUIRED. There is no second argument for the output PORT: noteout's channel encodes it \, so 33 reaches slot 3 exactly as 49 reaches slot 4. inlet 1: ONE inlet \, selector-prefixed -- pad <1..160> <velocity>. outlets: none \, everything it has to say goes on param \, disp and err., f 84;
#X text 900 20 160 PADS \, ONE FORMULA \, NO SPECIAL CASES. Bank sets the CHANNEL and pad sets the NOTE: banks A to J are the 404's own channels 1 to 10 \, which are Pd channels 33 to 42 \, and every bank uses the same sixteen notes 36 to 51. Pad 1 pressed on any bank reports note 48 \, with only the channel moving -- items 195 and 196., f 84;
#X text 1900 20 ⛔ 47 + n IS WRONG AND WAS IN THIS REPO'S OWN DOCS. It holds for pads 1 to 4 and then breaks: pad 5 is 44 \, not 52. The rows run DOWNWARD in blocks of four -- 48 49 50 51 on the top row \, then 44 45 46 47 \, then 40 41 42 43 \, then 36 37 38 39 at the bottom. Item 190., f 84;
#X text 20 3400 ONE TABLE \, BOTH DIRECTIONS \, WHICH IS THE WHOLE POINT. Receive searches field 1 for the note and reads back the pad \; transmit searches field 0 for the pad and reads back the note. The arithmetic happens to be self-inverse \, but two copies of a formula are two things that can drift -- and this map is the one this project has already got wrong once., f 66;
#X text 1220 3400 IT IS -k RATHER THAN A FILE \, unlike cut-it-map.txt next door \, and the difference is lifecycle: the pad map is a DEVICE FACT that is checked once and never edited \, while the mapping table is configuration that changes constantly. Same reasoning that gives u_err and u_state two files each., f 66;
#X text 2420 3400 THE CHANNEL GATE IS m_nano's \, TEN WIDE INSTEAD OF TWO \, and the offset IS the bank. Every other device in the rig falls outside it: the Launchpad sits 32 below and the Volca 16 above \, so nothing can be mistaken for a 404 pad. Banks use 33 to 42 and 43 to 48 stay unused., f 66;
#X text 20 3640 THE BANK LETTER IS TEN LITERAL MESSAGE BOXES \, not arithmetic on a character code -- so the ten names are ON THE CANVAS where a wrong one is visible. notein fires channel before pitch \, so the format is always set before the pad number arrives to use it. Verified in 0.49 that makefilename takes a set message on its LEFT inlet., f 66;
#X text 1220 3640 ONE STABLE disp NAME INSTEAD OF 160 \, AND IT NEEDS NO CLASSIFIER. A playing 404 pattern transmits notes exactly like a hand press -- same channel \, same range \, overlapping velocities (items 204 and 205) \, no side channel -- so telling them apart is NOT POSSIBLE and anyone who writes that test will be subtly wrong. But the problem was never rate \, it was DISTINCTNESS: g_oled holds five parameter rows and five different pad names evict everything else. sp-hit can never evict more than one row at any rate \, forever., f 66;
#X text 2420 3640 ⛔ AND THE disp VALUE MUST BE A FLOAT. g_oled turns a parameter value into a symbol with makefilename %g \, which REFUSES a symbol input -- so sp-hit b7 is impossible and sp-hit 7 is what goes. The bank is deliberately left off: the 404 shows its own selected bank on its own screen \, and a number you can read beats one you have to decode., f 66;
#X text 20 3880 EVERY EVENT GOES TO param AND ONLY A PRESS GOES TO disp. A note-off is a real event -- something downstream will want the release -- but a release is not worth a display row \, so the > 0 test sits on the disp side alone. Action first and report second \, off one trigger \, exactly like m_nano., f 66;
#X text 1220 3880 CC IN IS THE CTRL KNOBS \, named by RAW CC NUMBER rather than by guessed function -- sp-cc-16 and sp-cc-17. A generated name is honest where sp-filter would be a guess wearing a costume \, which is the argument m_launchpad already makes for its ring. These are gestures rather than sequencer traffic \, so they get both buses., f 66;
#X text 2420 3880 THE RATE LIMIT DROPS \, IT NEVER QUEUES \, and that is the whole design. Item 209 proved there is NO queue between Pd and the 404 -- and that overshooting costs SECONDS of lag that outlive the gesture \, while a stop is instant. A closed spigot emits nothing \, so the event is GONE rather than deferred: one vanilla object \, no construction \, and the first event of every window survives \, which is the right one for a trigger., f 66;
#X text 20 4120 5 ms IS 200 PER SECOND \, about half the measured ceiling of 360 to 400 (item 208) and fifteen times a sixteenth-note stream at 200 BPM. It sits BEFORE the note-off is scheduled \, so a dropped trigger can never leave an orphan note-off behind it., f 66;
#X text 1220 4120 ⛔ THE NOTE-OFF CARRIES ITS OWN CHANNEL \, AND makenote CANNOT DO THIS. m_volca uses makenote safely because the Volca has ONE channel set cold at load. The 404 has TEN. makenote schedules the off \, and by the time it fires noteout's cold channel inlet holds whatever the most recent event set -- so two banks overlapping inside the note duration send the off to the WRONG BANK. Silent \, plausible \, wrong. pipe carries note \, velocity and channel together \, and its three outlets fire RIGHT TO LEFT -- measured -- which hands noteout the channel before the note for free., f 66;
#X text 2420 4120 PANIC COVERS ALL TEN CHANNELS. u_tempo used to send All Notes Off on channel 33 alone \, which is bank A and one tenth of the instrument \, written before this file existed. The device's owner owns its panic -- the same argument m_launchpad makes for owning its own safe exit., f 66;
#X text 20 4360 SELF-IDENTIFYING \, like m_nano and m_volca. The 404 transmits plenty \, but nothing that says which Pd channel block it landed on \, and Pd 0.49 does not warn about a missing creation argument. ⚠️ The 2000 ms is tools/deploy.sh's rule -- it gates on OUTPUT and quits at about 735 ms., f 66;
#X text 1220 4360 THE REJECT IS A REAL ERROR \, exactly as in m_volca: an unrecognised selector means u_map and this file disagree about the interface. The t b is the reject-outlet rule -- a reject carries the DATA that failed to match \, never a bang., f 66;
#X obj 240 1020 + 1;
#X obj 240 1080 f;
#X obj 940 1560 t b b;
#X msg 940 1620 sp-bank \$1;
#X text 940 1700 TWO STABLE ROWS RATHER THAN ONE \, and the bank is the reason. sp-hit alone could not tell bank A pad 1 from bank B pad 1 -- the distinction was on param all along but never on the display. ⚠️ IT COULD NOT BE ONE ROW: g_oled formats a parameter value with makefilename %g \, which REFUSES a symbol \, so sp-hit b1 is impossible. Two names that never vary cost one more of the five rows and can still never evict anything at any rate \, which is the property that mattered., f 62;
#X obj 20 4620 c_devid 65;
#X obj 320 4620 r \$0-on;
#X obj 320 4680 select 1;
#X obj 620 4620 r \$0-cc-on;
#X obj 620 4680 select 1;
#X obj 20 4800 c_presence m_404 3 120;
#X msg 20 4880 240 \, 126 \, 127 \, 6 \, 1 \, 247;
#X obj 20 5100 midiout;
#X obj 320 4800 loadbang;
#X obj 320 4850 f \$1;
#X obj 320 4900 - 1;
#X obj 320 4950 div 16;
#X obj 320 5000 + 1;
#X text 900 4620 DEVICE PRESENCE. c_presence owns this device's last-heard clock and registers m_404 as active on the presence bus at load \; c_devid 65 matches Roland's manufacturer byte in a universal device inquiry reply. 65 is 0x41 -- item 249 \, measured on this unit. THE STAGGER IS 120 ms \, the largest of the three \, because one sysexin serves the whole patch and u_present broadcasts ONE tick that every c_presence hears in the same logical instant. Three inquiries leaving together can come back interleaved byte by byte \, which would hand c_devid one device's frame with another device's bytes in it. See ref/module/presence.md., f 62;
#X text 900 4920 ⛔ THE PORT IS DERIVED FROM THE CHANNEL BLOCK \, exactly as in m_nano. This file already makes the same point about noteout -- the channel encodes the port \, so 33 reaches slot 3 with no second argument. midiout is the one MIDI object that does NOT encode it that way: it takes the port as a plain number in its cold inlet \, so the arithmetic (n-1)/16+1 turns the block into the port. 33 gives 3., f 62;
#X text 1900 4620 TWO CHANNEL GATES \, SO TWO LIVENESS TAPS \, and neither costs any rewiring above this line. \$0-on is the note path and \$0-cc-on is the CTRL knob path \, both recomputed on every event \, and a receive with a select 1 turns either into evidence that this device is alive. ⚠️ A PLAYING PATTERN COUNTS \, and that is right rather than a loophole. The 404's sequencer transmits exactly like a hand press -- same channels \, overlapping velocities \, items 204 and 205 -- and this file already says telling them apart is NOT POSSIBLE. It does not need to be: a device that is transmitting is a device that is plugged in \, which is the only question presence asks., f 62;
#X text 1900 4980 c_presence's SECOND OUTLET IS UNCONNECTED HERE \, as in m_nano. Only m_launchpad has anything to do on the transition -- a grid it must stop painting. Everything this file holds is recomputed per event \, so nothing goes stale while the device is away. ⚠️ AND THE SCHEDULED NOTE-OFFS ARE DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE. Flushing pipe on a loss would be the wrong call: inside 200 ms the device may well be back and the off still matters \, and if it is not \, the off goes to a port with nothing listening and costs nothing. A stuck note is the 404's own panic path \, which is r panic above and not this., f 62;
